*I stare at the house, baffled at the absurd design used, and my eyes shine a bit. I stay behind staring for a bit as they talk. Then after they begin walking for it, I glance at them approaching, stare for a bit, then start walking away.*
(I am separating from the group. This happens before they get blocked by the guards. Yoruichi notices as soon as I start away, asks where I am going, then the rest turn to look, Orihime being the first to talk after. I turn to look at them. Orihime and Chad attempt to approach, with Uryu jogging closely behind trying to catch up, but I block them with an invisible forcefield, similiar to when I stopped the Koryu. Uryu still behind notices and asks what am I planning. Orihime gets upset, but Ichigo comes and puts a hand on her shoulder and just tells her to not bother, that I do not want them to follow me and whatever I want to do they won't be able to change my mind. They throw a few glances towardse and start walking back. After that just end, whatever happens on Kukkaku is no longer relevant for Mochi. Remember this all happens before the two guards appears, and Yoruichi just tells them to hurry up. Theyre in a plains. The last thing Mochi hears before she leaves is the two guards stopping them, talking something about Yoruichi and letting them in after recognizing Yoruichi.)

Liked:
*I stare at the house, at the two huge stone arms holding up their banner and the stack of chimney poking out of the roof. The design is so absurd that my eyes shine a little. I stay where I am at the back of the group and keep looking, and the voices ahead of me blur together.*

"Yoruichi-san," Uryū says, "what else have you not told us about her?"

"Nothing, nothing." Yoruichi flicks her tail. "Come on. Let's go."

Ichigo mutters something under his breath, and the group starts down the slope toward the house, with Uryū still holding the map in a death grip. Orihime trots after them, smiling nervously.

*I glance at their backs as they move off. I stare at them for a while. Then I turn around and begin walking the other way, away from the house, with the grass whispering against my legs.*

A few paces later, Yoruichi stops on Chad's shoulder. The cat's head turns, and the ears go flat. "Wait. Where are you going?"

The others pull up and look back.

"Mochi-chan?" Orihime is the first to speak. Her voice wavers. "Where are you going?"

*I stop and turn around to look at them.*

Orihime hurries toward me, with Chad following in long strides. Uryū jogs a few steps behind with the map crumpled in his fist, trying to catch up.

*I raise one hand.*

Orihime runs straight into something that isn't there. Her palms flatten against empty air, and she bounces back with a small yelp. Chad slows and puts out an arm and meets the same invisible wall, which doesn't so much as ripple under his hand. He stands there looking down at his own fingers, pressed flat against nothing.

Uryū stops short behind them. His eyes narrow. "That's the same thing as before, in the Dangai." He pushes his glasses up with the back of his wrist. "What are you planning?"

"Mochi-chan!" Orihime presses both hands to the invisible wall and looks at me with her eyes shining. "Why? Where are you going? You'll be all alone out there, and you don't even know the way..."

A hand lands on her shoulder.

Ichigo has come up behind her. He doesn't look angry, only tired, and his eyes rest on me for a long moment. Then he gives a small, sideways shake of his head.

"Leave it, Inoue. Don't bother."

"But Kurosaki-kun..."

"She doesn't want us to follow." He lets out a breath. "Whatever she wants to do, we won't be able to change her mind."

Orihime opens her mouth, then closes it. Her shoulders slump. Chad lowers his arm, and Uryū says nothing, but his gaze lingers on me before he turns.

They throw a few glances back as they go, and Ichigo's is the longest. Then Yoruichi's voice rises from Chad's shoulder, brisk and sharp. "Hurry up. We're wasting time."

*I watch them climb back up the slope and start toward the house. Then I turn around and keep walking.*
